e Sun has vanished (specifically, the Nourishing Sun) - taking all the actual sun\u2019s affect on the world (like heat, growing crops..) and they travel across the primeval wilderness to find and rescue the sun. With a nice twist that this Pangaean was in fact imprisoned by Atlanteans in the Time Before, but their temple projected its power across the world - so it was \u201cfine\u201d until the temple broke. So they have to fight a spirit of Hunger who broke the temple to start with, and escort the Sun out of the Death Swamp to where it can ascend back to the sky. And as a reward, they\u2019re given an Omphalos stone, told to keep its fire burning forever, and asked to create a cult devoted to the sun.<br /> I always tell an epilogue, to show its consequences spreading out to the future, where the flame has been tended six thousand years and, when destroyed by invaders, all of Europe suffers a century long famine just before getting hit by the Black Plague. Which is true ... the eternal flame being broken in ~1200 AD is probably a coincidence, but it makes for really good fiction.<br /> <br /> Very mythic, very classic fantasy adventure. I decided to write that type of story mostly to make it easier to jump people in as a one shot, but also because I really wanted practice for wilderness adventures (choosing routes, complications with rations, random encounters) - and then a whole heaping of \u201cPrincess Mononoke is awesome\u201d.<br /> And I based the setting and pangaeans on Lithuanian mythology - which I learned for another game, and pretty well fell in love with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For some specific stories that have come up from running this:<ul><li>They\u2019ve come across an Atlantean shrine in the mountains, holding an artifact that controlled the weather. Due almost entirely to about a dozen rolls of only exceptional success or dramatic failure, a Pangaean of storms coveted it, dragged them into the Border Marches, and they finally negotiated aide on their quest for it to keep the artifact.</li> <li>They\u2019ve come across a village people tried to settle without a Wise to protect them, all of whom became spirit claimed, and hunted by a werewolf pack - a pack they had to parlay with to pass through.</li> <li>They\u2019ve recruited a Wolf Blooded outlander from the Cult of the Hunter to accompany them.</li> <li>They came across a dead lands of Atlantean design, where ghosts were trapped in statues, presumably as some kind of border security or maybe from the place being ground down by dissonance. My players decided to actually <i>explore </i>that place, which wore them down a lot, but earned them an Artifact of death magic.</li> <li>They\u2019ve passed through a swamp village, far from their home valley, devoted to the pangaean Owl (unclean death), who had Proto-Vampires protecting them in place of Wise.</li> <li>And they met a bunny spirit who, with plants no longer gaining nutrients since the loss of the sun, pleaded with them to give it a knife so it could teach it\u2019s warren to hunt and eat meat instead. That was fun and unsettling; they took that as a nice kick to finish this quest before the natural order fell entirely to pieces.</li> </ul><br /> \u200bI\u2019ve used a lot of fun descriptions running this, particularly with Atlantean shrines, which had anachronistic technology like glass and thauminum manacles, and in the Border Marches - they\u2019ve been to both a mountain range, and to Owl\u2019s personal swamp of death. The intro scene is pretty well always fun, with four villages gathered together so that their Wise can perform the midsummer ritual - both religious and magical - and the role play that has happened from players having to break the news that they need to go on a quest, leaving everyone defenseless for who knows how long - but without causing mass hysteria.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sundered world is more or less my favorite setting ever. I\u2019ve had a long lasting love of historical fantasy - and I\u2019m pretty much a history / mythology / evolution nerd, so this hits so many of my passions (and things I\u2019ve actually studied!). I would love to run a longer chronicle of this, or even write some more one shots, but my ST hands are full right now. I\u2019d probably love being a player in Sundered World more.... or even it being a video game. It has some majestic descriptions that I\u2019d love to visually see, and it begs for exploration - which is fun as a ST, but more so as a PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a link to the scenario and Genesys rules? Would love that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T13:11:51-08:00","id":1349153,"title":"","content":"I have the barest bones write-ups I need to pull this off at the table; I do not have a full write up of the scenario, or even the rules. I may write this up as an SAS for the storyteller's vault at some point, but what I have on hand right now I don't think is fleshed out enough to be useful to someone else.<br /> <br /> Regarding the rules in particular, I don't run this scenario using the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/228813/Genesys-Core-Rulebook\" target=\"_blank\">Genesys</a> rules; I have been working on my own system hack that runs Fate Accelerated using the Genesys dice. And I've written some mods to play ChroD templates with those rules. It sounds like a <i>really</i> wonky hack when I put it like that, but it's meant to be really easy to pick up, and it's been a lot of fun for the one-shots I've ran.<br /> It's been a major project for me, but it's taken a back-burner recently as I've started up a new chronicle. I've done a good deal of playtesting, but it hasn't been fully drafted and polished to the point where I'd be ready to share it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}